  "text": " If you buy into the hypothesis that for some reason there are incentives for the government to maintain the state of emergency, that is one explanation given that those declarations are expiring and will have to be re-implemented because if they're not, then all of this emergency use authorization vanishes like dust. So are you saying or are you implying that perhaps one of the reasons why they're removing monoclonal antibodies is to enhance the amount of people that are sick? I'm saying it is in the spectrum of the range of possible just the same as the withholding of early treatments is inexplicable. And this is inexplicable in that we know that they're very effective. But I have personal evidence that they're very effective. They work great on me. The fact that they're removing this and that you would even consider that the reason why they're doing it is to extend the emergency use authorization for political reasons is that's insane. That's terrifying.",
